concept_mcqs.stem:
A bucket policy allows uploads only from the office IP range, breaking a Lambda integration that egresses via a NAT with dynamic IPs. Current bucket policy:
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "OfficeOnly",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": ["s3:PutObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::example-bucket/*",
      "Condition": {"IpAddress": {"aws:SourceIp": "203.0.113.0/24"}}
    }
  ]
}
```
The Lambda function role is `arn:aws:iam::111122223333:role/ingestor-lambda`. Choose the revision that preserves the office IP restriction for everyone else but restores ingestion from the Lambda role.

options:
Match the Lambda client by user agent:
```json
{
  "Condition": {"StringLike": {"aws:UserAgent": "*AWSLambda*"}}
}
```

Keep the policy and add a condition to rely on AWS internals:
```json
{
  "Condition": {"Bool": {"aws:ViaAWSService": "true"}}
}
```

concept_mcqs.stem:
Your security team adds this guardrail as a permission policy attached to all human IAM users to reduce risk/cost outside the EU:
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "DenyOutsideEU",
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Action": "*",
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringNotEqualsIfExists": {
          "aws:RequestedRegion": ["eu-west-1", "eu-central-1"]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```
Which call still succeeds for those users?

Group `Admins` has this policy to enforce MFA:
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Action": ["iam:DeleteUser", "iam:CreateAccessKey", "ec2:*", "s3:*", "rds:*", "*"],
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {"Bool": {"aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent": "false"}}
    }
  ]
}
```
An admin without MFA enabled sees `AccessDenied` when trying `ec2:StartInstances`. What action allows them to proceed without weakening the control?

